From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:28:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 28/79] server: engine-owned reply bytes survive every strip,
 at the format's own call openers

reply_owned.zig: an Owned span of a reply's content (where the engine's cell
writes landed) that no prose strip may cut. The strips take the reply's call
openers (reply_text.Openers, openersOf(markers)), so DSML is one format among
Qwen's <tool_call> JSON and XML, Gemma's, LFM2's and MiniMax's; an owned span
ends before the first call block either the stream or the parser sees.

- reply_owned.of projects cell-write records ({field, token, landed}) onto
  the content; content the server rewrote (MiniMax, LFM2 as DSML) owns none.
- tool_parse.parseOwned, tool_stream.endProseOwned, reply_owned.finishedProse
  and cutProse keep the owned bytes; with none owned each is the existing
  function, so no format's bytes change.
- Reply.owned and Generation.owned carry the span through the chat route,
  the compute lane's segments and the client's calls; nothing sets it until
  the runner feeds its cell writes.

Ported from the dsv41 release line's runner_owned.zig and reply_text.Owned.
